text: ['({T}: Add {B}.)', '({T}: Add {U}.)', '({T}: Add {W}.)', 'As an additional cost to cast this spell, exile a creature card from your graveyard.', 'As an additional cost to cast this spell, exile a creature card from your graveyard.\\nFlying', "As an additional cost to cast this spell, exile a creature card from your graveyard.\\nUndying (When this creature dies, if it had no +1/+1 counters on it, return it to the battlefield under its owner's control with a +1/+1 counter on it.)", 'Create five 1/1 white Human creature tokens. If this spell was cast from a graveyard, create ten of those tokens instead.\\nFlashback {7}{W}{W} (You may cast this card from your graveyard for its flashback cost. Then exile it.)', 'Create two 1/1 white Human creature tokens.\\nFateful hour — If you have 5 or less life, create five of those tokens instead.', 'Create two 2/2 black Zombie creature tokens.\\nFlashback {5}{B}{B} (You may cast this card from your graveyard for its flashback cost. Then exile it.)', 'Deathtouch\\nOther Zombie creatures you control get +1/+1.\\nWhenever another Zombie you control dies, target opponent loses 1 life.', 'Deathtouch\\nWhenever another nontoken creature dies, you may draw a card.', 'Destroy target Human creature.', 'Destroy target attacking creature.', 'Destroy target non-Vampire, non-Werewolf, non-Zombie creature.', 'Diregraf Ghoul enters the battlefield tapped.', 'Dismal Backwater enters the battlefield tapped.\\nWhen Dismal Backwater enters the battlefield, you gain 1 life.\\n{T}: Add {U} or {B}.', 'Draw three cards, untap up to two lands, then discard a card.', 'Each player sacrifices two creatures.', "Enchant creature\\nEnchanted creature gets +2/+2 as long as it's a Human. Otherwise, it can't attack or block.", 'Equipped creature gets +3/+0.\\nAs long as equipped creature is a Human, it has lifelink.\\nEquip {3}', 'Equipped creature has first strike.\\nAs long as equipped creature is a Human, it gets +1/+1.\\nEquip {1}', 'Equipped creature has flying.\\nEquip {1} ({1}: Attach to target creature you control. Equip only as a sorcery.)', "Exile any number of target creatures you control. Return those cards to the battlefield under their owner's control at the beginning of the next end step.", 'Exile target creature and all other creatures with the same name as that creature.\\nFlashback {5}{B}{B} (You may cast this card from your graveyard for its flashback cost. Then exile it.)', "Exile target creature you control, then return it to the battlefield under its owner's control.\\nFlashback {3}{U} (You may cast this card from your graveyard for its flashback cost. Then exile it.)", "First strike\\nWhenever a creature dealt damage by Abattoir Ghoul this turn dies, you gain life equal to that creature's toughness.", 'Flash (You may cast this spell any time you could cast an instant.)\\nWhen Village Bell-Ringer enters the battlefield, untap all creatures you control.', 'Flying', "Flying (This creature can't be blocked except by creatures with flying or reach.)\\nScrapskin Drake can block only creatures with flying.", 'Flying, trample\\nWhen Mindwrack Demon enters the battlefield, mill four cards.\\nDelirium — At the beginning of your upkeep, you lose 4 life unless there are four or more card types among cards in your graveyard.', 'Flying\\nAs long as Dearly Departed is in your graveyard, each Human creature you control enters the battlefield with an additional +1/+1 counter on it.', "Flying\\nWhen Emancipation Angel enters the battlefield, return a permanent you control to its owner's hand.", 'Flying\\nWhen Goldnight Redeemer enters the battlefield, you gain 2 life for each other creature you control.', 'Flying\\nWhen Gryff Vanguard enters the battlefield, draw a card.', "Flying\\nWhen Mist Raven enters the battlefield, return target creature to its owner's hand.", "Flying\\nWhen Topplegeist enters the battlefield, tap target creature an opponent controls.\\nDelirium — At the beginning of each opponent's upkeep, if there are four or more card types among cards in your graveyard, tap target creature that player controls.", 'Flying\\nWhen Tower Geist enters the battlefield, look at the top two cards of your library. Put one of them into your hand and the other into your graveyard.', 'Flying\\nWhen Voice of the Provinces enters the battlefield, create a 1/1 white Human creature token.', 'Flying\\nWhenever Falkenrath Noble or another creature dies, target player loses 1 life and you gain 1 life.', "Gravecrawler can't block.\\nYou may cast Gravecrawler from your graveyard as long as you control a Zombie.", "Hexproof (This creature can't be the target of spells or abilities your opponents control.)\\nWhenever Geist of Saint Traft attacks, create a 4/4 white Angel creature token with flying that's tapped and attacking. Exile that token at end of combat.", 'Look at the top four cards of your library. Put one of them into your hand and the rest into your graveyard.\\nFlashback {6}{B} (You may cast this card from your graveyard for its flashback cost. Then exile it.)', 'Return target creature card from your graveyard to the battlefield.\\nFlashback—Sacrifice three creatures. (You may cast this card from your graveyard for its flashback cost. Then exile it.)', "Return target nonland permanent to its owner's hand. Then that player discards a card if you control a Zombie.", 'Soulbond (You may pair this creature with another unpaired creature when either enters the battlefield. They remain paired for as long as you control both of them.)\\nAs long as Spectral Gateguards is paired with another creature, both creatures have vigilance.', 'Soulbond (You may pair this creature with another unpaired creature when either enters the battlefield. They remain paired for as long as you control both of them.)\\nAs long as Tandem Lookout is paired with another creature, each of those creatures has "Whenever this creature deals damage to an opponent, draw a card."', 'Target opponent reveals their hand. You choose a card from it with mana value 4 or greater and exile that card.', "Target opponent sacrifices a creature. You gain life equal to that creature's toughness.", 'Tranquil Cove enters the battlefield tapped.\\nWhen Tranquil Cove enters the battlefield, you gain 1 life.\\n{T}: Add {W} or {U}.', 'Unbreathing Horde enters the battlefield with a +1/+1 counter on it for each other Zombie you control and each Zombie card in your graveyard.\\nIf Unbreathing Horde would be dealt damage, prevent that damage and remove a +1/+1 counter from it.', "Undying (When this creature dies, if it had no +1/+1 counters on it, return it to the battlefield under its owner's control with a +1/+1 counter on it.)", 'When Cathedral Sanctifier enters the battlefield, you gain 3 life.', 'When Doomed Traveler dies, create a 1/1 white Spirit creature token with flying.', 'When Driver of the Dead dies, return target creature card with mana value 2 or less from your graveyard to the battlefield.', 'When Elder Cathar dies, put a +1/+1 counter on target creature you control. If that creature is a Human, put two +1/+1 counters on it instead.', "When Fiend Hunter enters the battlefield, you may exile another target creature.\\nWhen Fiend Hunter leaves the battlefield, return the exiled card to the battlefield under its owner's control.", 'When Ghoulraiser enters the battlefield, return a Zombie card at random from your graveyard to your hand.', 'When Screeching Skaab enters the battlefield, mill two cards.', 'When Seraph Sanctuary enters the battlefield, you gain 1 life.\\nWhenever an Angel enters the battlefield under your control, you gain 1 life.\\n{T}: Add {C}.', 'When Slayer of the Wicked enters the battlefield, you may destroy target Vampire, Werewolf, or Zombie.', "When Tooth Collector enters the battlefield, target creature an opponent controls gets -1/-1 until end of turn.\\nDelirium — At the beginning of each opponent's upkeep, if there are four or more card types among cards in your graveyard, target creature that player controls gets -1/-1 until end of turn.", 'Whenever another Human enters the battlefield under your control, put a +1/+1 counter on Champion of the Parish.', 'Whenever another Human enters the battlefield under your control, untap Captain of the Mists.\\n{1}{U}, {T}: You may tap or untap target permanent.', '{2}{U}, {T}, Exile a creature card from your graveyard: Create a 2/2 black Zombie creature token, then put a +1/+1 counter on each Zombie creature you control.', '{2}{W}: Moorland Inquisitor gains first strike until end of turn. (It deals combat damage before creatures without first strike.)', '{3}{U}, {T}: Exile another target creature you control, then return that card to the battlefield under your control.', '{T}: Exile target creature card from a graveyard.']
flavor: ['"\'I\'m certain that the fate of Markov Manor is connected to these cryptoliths . . .\' This Tamiyo was on to something."', '"At least this one still has arms and legs. Well, most of its legs."\\n—Enslow, ghoulcaller of Nephalia', '"Come. Bring your brothers. Tonight, you feast on living flesh."\\n—Jadar, ghoulcaller of Nephalia', '"Do not touch a drop. Not yet. I want to watch this so-called slayer\'s last crisis of faith."\\n—Olivia Voldaren', '"Evil will soon be vanquished. What Innistrad most needs now is healing."', '"Ghouls smashed the door, but I heard the call of the gryffs and knew we were saved."\\n—Ekka, shopkeeper of Hanweir', '"He is judge, jury, and executioner because he killed them all."\\n—Bishop Cawle of Elgaud', '"I am no mere ship\'s captain. The north wind is my accomplice. The tide is my first mate."', '"I have seen a hundred mortal families rise and fall. I shall outlast a thousand more."\\n—Olivia Voldaren', '"I often think on how excited they must feel to be chosen as my prey."', '"I stand for every cobbler, tanner, and fool in this town—and they stand for me."', '"Innistrad\'s ghoulcallers are talented enough, but let me show you what someone with real power can create."\\n—Liliana Vess', '"It always amazes me what perfectly good things people throw away."\\n—Ludevic, necro-alchemist', '"Let them decry me for burning the dead. I\'m not giving those ghoulcallers any more fuel for their madness."', '"My drivers are trustworthy. I removed their tongues myself. Any other questions?"', '"My greatest hope is that you will surpass me in every way, consigning my name to some forgotten corner of history."', '"Never forget our ancestors. They have not forgotten us."\\n—Mikaeus, the Lunarch', '"No one chooses to be stitched together into a skaab. If it could speak, it would beg for its own destruction."\\n—Thalia, Knight-Cathar', '"Priests, hunters, slayers—to arms! The enemy approaches!"', '"So many corpses, so little time."', '"So much for neighborly hospitality!"', '"The best skaabs are more powerful and more beautiful than the sum of their parts."\\n—Stitcher Geralf', '"The cathars killed my skaabs down below. Let\'s see how high their swords can reach."\\n—Ludevic, necro-alchemist', '"We must all make sacrifices for the good of Innistrad."\\n—Sorin Markov', '"What cannot be destroyed will be bound."\\n—Oath of Avacyn', '"When you see a raven, head for the hills. It knows when the ghost-tide is headed in."\\n—Sved, fisherman of Nephalia', '"You have done your best. I give you leave to rest."', 'Death has bound it with chains of past regrets. Forever it searches for atonement, each kindness removing a single link.', 'Death took his humanity but not his skill with the knife.', 'For a ghoul, every village is a buffet and every disaster is a reunion.', 'For the necro-alchemist, any puzzle can be solved with intelligence and harvested body parts.', "He vowed he would never rest until he reached his destination. He doesn't know how right he was.", 'Her horn is heard across Innistrad, lifting the hearts of the righteous.', 'In the memories of those they lost lies the strength needed to defend their city.', 'Inquisitors are taught scripture, philosophy, and the fine art of sharpening an axe.', 'Its screeching is the sound of you losing your mind.', "Jenrik's tower is served by those who once sought to enter it uninvited.", 'Just as with a peach, the first bite is always the juiciest.', 'Marella was delighted. The ball had attracted so many suitors for her daughter, including that handsome stranger. She wondered where the two were now . . . .', 'Not everyone can have a sword of blessed silver. Not everyone needs one, either.', 'Outside the safety of Thraben, there is little distinction between tool and weapon.', 'Some vampires resorted to corpse trading after cathars burned their estates and drove them from their ancestral feeding grounds.', "The Host sings of Avacyn's return without a single verse about its own suffering.", 'The barrier between existence and oblivion is thinner than you know.', 'The will to return can overpower the will to survive.', 'Though its mind has long since rotted away, it wields a sword with deadly skill.', "Without a mind, it doesn't fear death. Without a soul, it doesn't mind killing.", "You don't want to see his trophy room."]
artist: ['Adam Paquette', 'Allen Williams', 'Anthony Palumbo', 'Bud Cook', 'Chris Rahn', 'Christopher Moeller', 'Clint Cearley', 'Daarken', 'Dan Murayama Scott', 'Daniel Ljunggren', 'Dave Kendall', 'David Palumbo', 'David Rapoza', 'Eric Deschamps', 'Evan Shipard', 'Eytan Zana', 'Igor Kieryluk', 'Izzy', 'James Paick', 'James Ryman', 'Jason Chan', 'Jason Felix', 'John Avon', 'Jung Park', 'Karl Kopinski', 'Kev Walker', 'Lars Grant-West', 'Magali Villeneuve', 'Matt Stewart', 'Michael C. Hayes', 'Nils Hamm', 'Peter Mohrbacher', 'Sam Burley', 'Scott Chou', 'Seb McKinnon', 'Slawomir Maniak', 'Steve Argyle', 'Steve Prescott', 'Steven Belledin', 'Svetlin Velinov', 'Volkan Baǵa', 'Wayne England', 'Wayne Reynolds', 'Winona Nelson']
